    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for today is headlined by **Daulton Varsho** (69.56) and **Taylor Ward** (68.88), who stand as our most reliable assets against favorable pitching matchups. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.58 xERA), and despite a slight drag from M\u00e1rquez\u2019s efficiency at holding runners, the pure upside of this platoon advantage puts him at the top of our daily projections. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** gains substantial value from a +16% park factor bump against Lugo, and his spot in the #2 hole ensures maximum plate appearance exposure. **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Luis Arraez** (65.86) also provide high-floor production, with **Luis Arraez** in particular seeing his efficiency score bolstered by an +18% boost due to the matchup against Lorenzen.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Bryce Harper** (50.42) on the bench. While his individual xwOBA remains elite at .394, the daunting prospect of facing Skubal\u2014who commands an elite 2.69 xERA\u2014effectively neutered his base projection, pushing him behind the higher-upside, favorable-matchup plays like **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.57) and **Jonathan Aranda** (55.23). Elsewhere, we are keeping a close eye on **Tyler Freeman** (49.94); while his scoring is marginal, the 88% stolen base allowance of his opposing pitcher, McDonald, makes him a sneaky leverage play in our quest to close the gap in the scarce SB category. **Cal Raleigh** (52.07) and **JJ Bleday** (53.63) round out the lineup, though both face risk from tougher left-handed starters, leaving them closer to our floor than our ceiling for today\u2019s slate.",
